---
// Sveltia CMS admin page.
//
// Sveltia CMS is the drop-in successor to Decap/Netlify CMS. It reads the same
// /public/admin/config.yml and auto-initialises on load, so this page only has
// to load the Sveltia bundle — no manual init, no YAML pre-parsing.
//
// WHAT CHANGED FROM THE OLD DECAP ADMIN PAGE (and why):
//  - Removed the Netlify Identity widget. Sveltia uses the GitHub backend
//    (see config.yml), so login is "Sign in with GitHub", not email invites.
//  - Removed the role-based collection filter. That relied on Netlify Identity
//    roles, which go away with the GitHub backend. Everyone invited to the repo
//    with Write access can edit every collection. (Sveltia has no per-user role
//    system yet; this is the accepted trade-off of the switch.)
//  - Removed the custom Google Maps pin-picker script + the Maps API key inject.
//    Sveltia doesn't support Decap custom widgets yet, so the coordinate field
//    is now a plain text box (config.yml). google-map-widget.js is left in the
//    repo, unused, in case we return to a CMS that supports it.
//
// TO GO LIVE: the GitHub backend needs an OAuth path so editors can sign in.
// On Netlify, enable the GitHub OAuth provider under
//   Site configuration -> Access & security -> OAuth -> Install provider (GitHub).
// (This is Netlify's plain GitHub OAuth app — NOT Netlify Identity/Git Gateway.)
// Alternatively, host Sveltia's tiny OAuth worker on Cloudflare and point
// `base_url`/`auth_endpoint` at it in config.yml. Either way, once OAuth is
// wired up, committee members invited to the repo can log in at /admin.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>KERNO admin</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/assets/cornwall-logo.png" />
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Sveltia CMS. `is:inline` stops Astro from bundling/deferring the tag, so
       it loads and auto-initialises against /admin/config.yml exactly as the
       Sveltia docs describe. -->
  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/@sveltia/cms/dist/sveltia-cms.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
